<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George of Antioch</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1151/52</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> was a Greek Christian who served the Zirid rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdia">Mahdia</a> before becoming the leading minister and admiral of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roger-ii-of-sicily">Roger II of Sicily</a>, with the title emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a>. His fleets captured Tripoli in 1146 and Mahdia in 1148, creating a short-lived Sicilian dominion in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>, and raided Corfu, Thebes and Corinth in 1147. He founded the church of Santa Maria dell'Ammiraglio in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Palermo</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-of-antioch.jpg" alt="George of Antioch" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rabe! · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Santa_Maria_dell%E2%80%99Ammiraglio_2015-03-28u.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
